I have enclosed a photocopy of your letter to me dated July 8, 1977. First, I want to thank you for your suggestions and the addresses of possible publishers. I followed up, no funds are available for a work such as mine, though they are interested in what I have done and would appreciate a copy of the folk song finder and index. It is a voluminous work, so I can understand the reluctance of a publisher to undertake the expense of its publication. So here I am, back to you again.
这是一个绝望之举。如果您真的有意让图书馆与我达成某种协议，我已经准备好推进了。我的问题是这样的，在给我的经济报酬方面，我不知道该要求多少。我确实知道，我不能要求弥补我所花费的时间、工作和金钱，但我希望能收回至少一部分我自己的支出，哪怕不是对我工作和时间的报酬。事实上，我必须收回我所花费的一些钱，因为我已经签下了加利福尼亚州波特维尔的一个小农场和房子的租约，预计在大约六周内搬到那里。正如乡村音乐界所说的那样，我已经身无分文了。莱利从未得到他所寻求的东西。

57
00:35:27.000 --> 00:36:16.000
It was an act of desperation. If you were our serious about the library reaching some agreement with me, I am ready to proceed. My problem is this, I don't know what to ask for in terms of financial remuneration to myself. I do know that I cannot ask as much as I have spent in terms of time, work, and money, but I would like to recoup at least some of my own expenditures, if not payment, for my work and time. In fact, I must recoup some of what I have spent because I have already signed a lease on a small farm and house in Porterville, California, and expect to move there in approximately six weeks. As I am, as they say in the country music field, flat busted. Riley never got what he was seeking.
他所要求的是一大笔资金投入，我认为图书馆当时实在承担不起，或者无法……你知道的，为那个项目拨出这笔款项。因为正如他在信中所说，除了这些卷宗之外，这本书还有另外54卷。另外54卷。经过近二十年苦心孤诣的工作，最终迎来了极大的侮辱。拒绝。

58
00:36:16.000 --> 00:36:47.000
What he was asking was a significant outlay of money that I just think the library couldn't afford at the time or couldn't, you know, a portion to that project. Because as he says in the correspondence, in addition to these volumes, there are 54 other volumes of this book. 54 other volumes. After nearly two decades of painstaking work came the final indignity. Rejection.
是的，我想你可以说他是从出版书籍（即纸质书）向电脑文档转变过程中的早期牺牲品。而且他意识到了这一点。我的意思是，因为他谈到了如果能把这些输入电脑该有多好。你会说莱利·谢帕德是个天才吗？我想他是个天才。我的意思是，看到他在这个项目上所做的工作量，真的非常令人印象深刻。而且他身上也具备那种你必须拥有的疯狂毅力。所以你知道，那是另一种天才。

