After Riley died, my dad had a little record player in his office, and he would put on a lot of Riley's country-western music. It was fun while it lasted, but it didn't last too long. You've left me for somebody new. And he just enjoyed Riley and enjoyed his friendship. But darling, I still believe in you. Won't you please come back and know I love you to the end? When Ted Enselin died, Steve gave the encyclopedia to another man in town who happened to be a country music songwriter. Steve says he was told the pages of carefully indexed entries were eventually split up.
