When an old man's in love, he just thinks he's in love. He's not cooking with gas, he's just warming it over. It's a good song, right? Songs and novels are filled with stories about people with great obsessions. We have strong opinions about such people. When they succeed, when they produce the Taj Mahal or Hamlet or the iPhone, we hail the obsessions that build the monuments of this world. When we count the collateral damage that people with obsessions leave in their wake, especially when those obsessions only produce the unreadable tom on the evil eye or an unpublishable encyclopedia on folk music.
当一个老头陷入爱河时，他只是觉得自己陷入爱河了。他并不是在动真格，他只是在重温旧梦。这是一首好歌，对吧？歌曲和小说里充满了关于有着巨大执念的人的故事。我们对这样的人有着强烈的看法。当他们成功时，当他们建造了泰姬陵、写出了《哈姆雷特》或是发明了iPhone时，我们为建立这个世界丰碑的执念欢呼。当我们计算那些有执念的人在身后留下的附带损害时——尤其是当这些执念只催生出关于邪眼的不可读皇皇巨著，或是关于民歌的无法出版的百科全书时，

